From ce6faaedef68204e8b132bf44a0e4d2432dfb7ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun-Prasad-V <arun.prasad.v@intel.com>
Date: Mon, 4 Nov 2024 12:52:39 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Support for dynamic change of i2c bus-clk-rate

Provide i2c_{set,get}_adapter_bus_clk_rate() for the D4XX DFU path.

These accessors must NOT add a member to struct i2c_adapter. Doing so
changes the genksyms CRC of every exported i2c-core symbol that
references struct i2c_adapter, which breaks loading of prebuilt
out-of-tree modules (notably the BSP NVIDIA display stack: nvidia.ko /
nvidia-modeset.ko / nvidia-drm.ko) on the patched kernel with
"disagrees about version of symbol" errors.

On Tegra the controller clock is programmed from i2c_timings.bus_freq_hz
via clk_set_rate(); adap->bus_clk_rate was never consumed by the bus
driver, so the value had no hardware effect. The accessors are therefore
ABI-neutral stubs that satisfy the D4XX call sites without touching the
public struct.

Signed-off-by: Arun Prasad V <arun.prasad.v@intel.com>
---
 drivers/i2c/i2c-core-base.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 include/linux/i2c.h         |  4 ++++
 2 files changed, 23 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/i2c/i2c-core-base.c b/drivers/i2c/i2c-core-base.c
index c232535ca8f4..2edd24973cca 100644
--- a/drivers/i2c/i2c-core-base.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/i2c-core-base.c
@@ -1401,6 +1401,26 @@ static int i2c_setup_host_notify_irq_domain(struct i2c_adapter *adap)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * i2c_{set,get}_adapter_bus_clk_rate() exist for the D4XX DFU path. They are
+ * intentionally ABI-neutral stubs: storing a rate in struct i2c_adapter would
+ * change the CRC of every exported i2c-core symbol and break loading of
+ * prebuilt modules (e.g. the BSP NVIDIA display stack). On Tegra the bus clock
+ * comes from i2c_timings.bus_freq_hz via clk_set_rate(), so this value had no
+ * hardware effect anyway.
+ */
+int i2c_set_adapter_bus_clk_rate(struct i2c_adapter *adap, int bus_rate)
+{
+	return 0;
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(i2c_set_adapter_bus_clk_rate);
+
+int i2c_get_adapter_bus_clk_rate(struct i2c_adapter *adap)
+{
+	return 0;
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(i2c_get_adapter_bus_clk_rate);
+
 /**
  * i2c_handle_smbus_host_notify - Forward a Host Notify event to the correct
  * I2C client.
diff --git a/include/linux/i2c.h b/include/linux/i2c.h
index 2ce3efbe9198..9d876ad6373c 100644
--- a/include/linux/i2c.h
+++ b/include/linux/i2c.h
@@ -131,6 +131,10 @@ int i2c_transfer(struct i2c_adapter *adap, struct i2c_msg *msgs, int num);
 /* Unlocked flavor */
 int __i2c_transfer(struct i2c_adapter *adap, struct i2c_msg *msgs, int num);
 
+/* Change bus clock rate for i2c adapter */
+extern int i2c_set_adapter_bus_clk_rate(struct i2c_adapter *adap, int bus_rate);
+extern int i2c_get_adapter_bus_clk_rate(struct i2c_adapter *adap);
+
 /* This is the very generalized SMBus access routine. You probably do not
    want to use this, though; one of the functions below may be much easier,
    and probably just as fast.
--
2.34.1
